#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:5
#: e2b3e27e0b5e44d7a27005e87105c56e
msgid "Camera Control in Auto Missions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:7
#: de2f5a5132fb4c2ba9d6102a23004f38
msgid "This article describes ArduPilot's camera and gimbal commands, and explains how these can be used in Mission Planner to define camera survey missions.  These instructions assume a :ref:`camera trigger and gimbal have already been connected and configured <common-cameras-and-gimbals>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:12
#: 2c8ad21292c146ccb4624e09159b10e8
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:14
#: 57d2553ae6a940bf81f4b14bb52263f9
msgid "Planning a camera mission is almost exactly the same as :ref:`planning any other mission with waypoints and events <common-planning-a-mission-with-waypoints-and-events>`. The only difference is that in a camera mission you specify commands to trigger the camera shutter at waypoints or at regular intervals as the vehicle moves. If the camera is mounted on a gimbal, you can also set the gimbal orientation, or make it track a particular point of interest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:20
#: 24581795d8e24d599dc5744e049fc011
msgid "For simple missions you can manually specify the required waypoints and camera commands. For more complex paths and grid surveys Mission Planner makes things easy by providing tools to automatically generating the required mission for arbitrary regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:26
#: 501d54aae501456f8d556f8d9aa76960
msgid "Camera commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:28
#: 86b6c929be204b15a77ae0016eafe5f0
msgid "``DO_SET_CAM_TRIGG_DIST`` — Trigger the camera shutter at regular intervals. This is most commonly used for supporting area surveys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:30
#: 1e2ebe6ca9e44bf881f8e5473a97585e
msgid "``DO_DIGICAM_CONTROL`` — Trigger the camera shutter once every time this command is called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:32
#: 5241938e934c4d73b811a7340b9002d8
msgid "``DO_AUX_FUNCTION`` — allows any :ref:`auxiliary function <common-auxiliary-functions>` to be executed from within a mission without setting up an auxiliary switch.  This includes camera start recording, camera zoom, camera manual focus and camera auto focus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:35
#: 81297b7d2d4f4baf8147fb0005cff600
msgid "Camera gimbal commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:37
#: 679e149196ea4d5dbba1dcc5c504c2c1
msgid "If a camera gimbal is used, you can set the camera position (yaw, tilt, roll) or aim it at a specific region of interest (ROI):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:40
#: 3ed57628784d4bb4b1f42310205c5568
msgid "``DO_SET_ROI`` — Target the camera towards a specified region of interest (position, including altitude)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:42
#: 6793b8480fdb4d608bd9cc2a3fdc17fe
msgid "``DO_GIMBAL_MANAGER_PITCHYAW`` — Move the gimbal to the desired pitch and yaw angles (in degrees).  Positive pitch angles are up, Negative are down.  Positive yaw angles are clockwise, negative are counter clockwise.   If the \"Flags\" field is \"0\" the yaw angle is in \"body frame\" (e.g. 0 is forward).  If \"Flags\" is \"16\" the yaw angle is in \"earth frame\" (e.g. 0 is North)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:43
#: 5953a20ba7914e2fa3bcd06d61df6cc6
msgid "``DO_MOUNT_CONTROL`` — Position the gimbal with the specified roll, pitch and yaw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:47
#: 1ac1073bf8e243f696663a05831e4700
msgid "Servo and Relay commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:49
#: 04903bbd735847a2a9420496e0490a6e
msgid "Servos and relay outputs can be connected to hardware and activated during missions using the ``DO_SET_SERVO`` or ``DO_SET_RELAY`` commands, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:53
#: c58a146ac186492dbe1176e8075b088b
msgid "One possible use for these outputs is to control camera features other than the shutter (for example, to set the zoom level or switch capture from still to video)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:59
#: 64f8952ca29e4a6f96e7f8fae87d7435
msgid "The method used to connect your servo or relay to the camera, and what features are accessible, will depend the camera and its supported remote-control mechanism(s) (see the :ref:`Camera Control and GeoTagging section of the Cameras and Gimbals wiki page <common-cameras-and-gimbals>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:64
#: 9d1b2559b5c54096941c2b5949b5aa46
msgid "Auto-mission types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-control-and-auto-missions-in-mission-planner.rst:66
#: f73b78555fd046ef9be3f918bb56e307
msgid "Mission Planner supports the following *Auto Waypoint* options. To access these open the *Flight Plan* screen, right-click on the map and select the option from under the *Auto WP* menu:"
msgstr ""

